# Architecture

Do not scan the repo to rediscover this map. Open the file you will edit.

## Packages

- `sailbrowser-web` — Angular app. Routes in `src/app/app.routes.ts`. Features live in `src/app/<feature>` (`model`, `services`, `presentation`). Import a model or service from the file that defines it. A function used only inside its feature lives in `*.helpers.ts`. Import a presentation component from its own file. Existing barrels may stay until a change touches them.
- `firebase/functions` — Cloud Functions. Register exports in `src/index.ts`. Defaults in `src/global-function-options.ts` (`europe-west1`, App Check).
- `home-site` — public site. `shared/contracts` — types shared across apps (`@shared/...`).
- Firestore data is club-scoped: `clubs/{clubId}/...`.

## Web routes

These paths load the folder of the same name: `home`, `entry`, `boats`, `events`, `race-calendar`, `results-input`, `results-sheet-phone-capture`, `sys-admin`, `club-admin`, `auth`, `user`. `results` loads `published-results`. `club` loads `club-tenant`. `scoring`, `shared`, `duties`, `system-data`, and `club-onboarding` are libraries with no `APP_ROUTES` entry. Club onboarding opens at `club-admin/onboarding`. Series scoring runs in the client (`app/scoring`, function `score`). Cloud Functions do not score races. `interpretSailingInstructions` reads sailing-instruction text. `fetchSailwaveResults` fetches a public results address and the Sailwave pages it links to, on the club's site or sailwave.com. Neither function scores races, parses result tables, or writes the club.

## Keep this file current

When a change adds or removes a package, feature folder, `APP_ROUTES` entry, function export, Firestore collection, or race type, update the matching file under `.cursor/rules/` in that same change. Do not add another architecture markdown file. If code and a rule disagree, change the rule to match the code.
